# No frontend environment file is required for local or Firebase Hosting use.
#
# Local development reads the backend's root .env through the Vite proxy. Start the backend with
# `uv run uvicorn cooper.app:app --reload --host 127.0.0.1`, then run `npm run dev` here.
#
# Firebase Hosting supplies its public Firebase Web configuration through
# `/__/firebase/init.json`; those values are not secrets and do not belong in a user setup file.
# A non-Firebase static host can provide the same public values through `window.__COOPER_CONFIG__`.
